WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.067
A Chinese

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:03.069
spy balloon is

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:04.804
hovering over the United States.

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:06.573
It was spotted high above Montana,

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:07.173
where the U.S.

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:09.876
military has a nuclear missile silo

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:11.778
The Pentagon is tracking this problem

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:12.545
closely and says

00:00:12.545 --> 00:00:14.180
it does not pose a military

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.115
or physical threat.

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:15.482
We're told

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:18.385
the balloon is the size of three busses.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:19.185
A senior defense

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:19.853
official says

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:20.520
President Biden

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.622
has been advised to not shoot it down

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.057
because the falling debris

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:25.825
could hurt people on the ground.

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:27.660
The balloons discovery is rattling

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:28.395
Capitol Hill.

00:00:28.395 --> 00:00:28.762
We're now

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:29.996
learning that staff members

00:00:29.996 --> 00:00:30.764
for the Gang of Eight

00:00:30.764 --> 00:00:32.132
have received a briefing.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.066
Joining us now on all of

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:34.467
this is our chief national security

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.435
correspondent, Jim Sciutto.

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:38.138
Jim, good morning. Wow.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:40.340
Listen, it's a slow moving Chinese

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.841
surveillance balloon

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.710
floating over the Continental.

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.811
Continental the U.S.

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:46.413
is understandably disturbing.

00:00:46.413 --> 00:00:46.980
My understanding

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:47.881
is that as of last night,

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.849
it hadn't left us airspace.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:50.984
So here's what we know so far.

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:51.317
First of all,

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:51.985
this is an image

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:52.986
captured from the ground.

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:54.954
It was visible with the naked eye

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:55.555
flying at about

00:00:55.555 --> 00:00:57.390
65,000 feet, about twice

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.659
as high as commercial aircraft.

00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:01.127
But much lower than

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.762
surveillance satellites,

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:03.496
as you were saying,

00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:05.832
going in the size of three busses.

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:08.301
Two flights were diverted for safety.

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.770
Military leaders considered,

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.006
but ultimately decided against

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:14.541
the president's decision

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:15.575
to shoot it down.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:16.543
But the idea

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:17.911
that that was under consideration

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.213
shows just how seriously

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:21.314
US officials

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:24.084
and the president were taking the idea

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:26.186
of a Chinese spy

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:28.088
balloon floating over the US.

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:29.389
You mentioned what it was flying

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:30.390
over, right,

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.525
Montana Malmstrom Air Base

00:01:32.692 --> 00:01:34.127
that has ICBMs there.

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:36.262
So something that China would

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:37.530
naturally be interested

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.731
in taking a closer look at.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:39.899
This happened before. Jim?

00:01:40.934 --> 00:01:41.701
It has.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.603
It has happened before over U.S.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:45.305
territory before.

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:46.005
But here's something

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:46.773
I do want to note

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.808
in terms of surveillance capabilities.

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:51.211
This was not a big jump in

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:52.779
what China is able to see.

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:53.413
Why is that?

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:55.682
Because China is flying spy satellites

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.250
over the US.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.319
Every 90 minutes is the orbit the Earth.

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:02.222
And those satellites have at least equal

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:03.990
surveillance capabilities.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.058
They're highly advanced.

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:07.193
So in terms of what China could gather

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.561
from this balloon,

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:10.196
not an enormous step forward.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:11.598
And by the way, we should note this,

00:02:11.598 --> 00:02:12.699
and this is something to be concerned

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:13.266
about,

00:02:13.266 --> 00:02:16.069
is that China is one of the most active

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:18.104
in terms of launching new satellites

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:19.172
Just look at the growth

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:20.206
going back to just six

00:02:20.206 --> 00:02:22.108
single digits in the 2000.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:24.244
Now they're up close to 100 per year.

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:25.378
The only other country

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:26.079
competing with that,

00:02:26.079 --> 00:02:27.413
frankly, is the U.S..

00:02:27.413 --> 00:02:28.381
And as you add it all

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.150
up, in terms of satellites,

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.152
China is second to the U.S.

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:32.519
in terms

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:34.154
of what they have floating

00:02:34.154 --> 00:02:35.188
above there right now.

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:36.823
Again, all looking down at the US

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:39.125
gathering intelligence is all the time.

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:40.493
I spoke to a number of U.S.

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:41.461
officials last night.

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.196
So this is not a big gain

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:44.797
in terms of surveillance,

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:46.966
but it is in terms of audacity

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.202
to fly a slow moving

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.203
surveillance balloon

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:51.271
over the continent,

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:54.440
not continental US and no the US.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.008
The president,

00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:57.076
you and I could see it as it's happening.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:57.510
Yeah.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.946
And just before the Secretary of State,

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:00.680
Antony Blinken,

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:01.347
goes to meet

00:03:01.347 --> 00:03:03.716
with high ranking Chinese officials.

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:05.351
Certainly going to change the discussion

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.886
there, Jim. Absolutely.

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:08.288
And by the way, as you know, Poppy,

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:10.190
those decisions are not made by accident.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:12.392
You can see that perhaps a message

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:12.992
to the U.S.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:13.693
secretary of state

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:14.861
as he prepares to go to Beijing.

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:16.996
All right, Jim, thank you very much.

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.498
Joining us now for more perspective on

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:19.632
this is the former defense

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:20.733
secretary under former

00:03:20.733 --> 00:03:22.468
President Trump, Mark Esper.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.103
Thank you so much for being here with us

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:24.671
this morning.

00:03:24.671 --> 00:03:26.973
I guess the number one question I have is

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:29.042
when the White House makes the decision

00:03:29.042 --> 00:03:30.243
not to shoot it down,

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.511
do you agree with that decision?

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:33.046
What kind of options do they have here?

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.182
Well,

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:38.117
first of all, I'm surprised by this.

00:03:38.117 --> 00:03:39.619
I think it is a brazen act

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:42.121
by the Chinese to do this.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.323
We were just talking about

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:43.790
whether or not

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.658
it has more or less intelligence value

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:47.093
than what they currently have.

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:48.895
I don't think we know.

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:50.697
And so my interest would be

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:52.298
not necessarily shooting it down,

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:54.367
but bringing bringing it down.

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.236
So that we can capture the equipment

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:57.804
and understand exactly what they do.

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:59.539
They're doing are they taking pictures?

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:00.974
Are they intercepting signals?

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:01.774
What are they doing?

00:04:01.774 --> 00:04:03.176
And what is the level

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:04.611
of technical capability?

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:05.645
It will tell us a lot

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:06.913
about what they're trying to do.

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.081
What they're trying to learn

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:09.649
and what their capability is of

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:10.617
doing that now.

00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:11.284
Failing that,

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:13.152
I would definitely shoot it down

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.320
provided that there's no risk

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.955
to people on the ground. Yeah.

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:17.257
So you are surprised

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:19.292
that this is just hovering over the

00:04:19.325 --> 00:04:20.493
continental U.S.

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:23.763
Oh, absolutely.

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.365
Not just the continental United States,

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:26.332
but over our,

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:27.567
you know, our missile fields

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.135
and our strategic bomber bases.

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:30.570
And so that's a great concern to me

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:31.271
that they are collecting

00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:32.805
intelligence and look,

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:34.507
they obviously are looking for something.

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:36.175
They need information that I would assume

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:38.011
they can't get through satellites.

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:39.212
And so that's why I would be

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:41.281
very interested in getting hold of this.

00:04:41.281 --> 00:04:42.849
Whatever the payload is

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:43.583
and understanding

00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:45.351
exactly what they're looking for and why.

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.019
And then, of course,

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:47.420
it gives us a good sense of their level

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.088
of technological capability.

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:50.456
The Chinese have been spying on us

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:51.491
for years, for decades.

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:52.091
We know

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:53.192
the FBI tells us

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:54.360
that, what, every 12 hours

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:56.195
they open up an espionage case.

00:04:56.195 --> 00:04:58.064
To me, this is a brazen act.

00:04:58.064 --> 00:04:59.399
And so at the political level,

00:04:59.399 --> 00:05:00.300
we have to push back.

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:02.268
We have to defend American sovereignty,

00:05:02.268 --> 00:05:04.203
and we have to make clear to the Chinese

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:05.905
that we're not going to tolerate this.

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:07.206
Is that your sense of why

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:08.841
it would be flying over Montana

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:09.976
because of that air base

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:11.377
that maintains and operates

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:12.612
those intercontinental

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:13.479
ballistic missiles?

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:16.449
Well, that would be my first guest.

00:05:16.449 --> 00:05:17.216
But until we know what

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:18.251
type of instrumentation

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:19.652
they have in the payload,

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:20.553
we wouldn't know for sure.

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:21.554
There are other facilities

00:05:21.554 --> 00:05:23.222
or things we do

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:24.557
in that part of the country.

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:25.825
So that's why I would want to get

00:05:25.825 --> 00:05:27.093
a hold that technology and find out.

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:27.727
But again,

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:29.162
that's at the intelligence level.

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:30.029
At the political level,

00:05:30.029 --> 00:05:30.363
we have to

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:31.764
send a very strong message back

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:33.433
that we won't tolerate this behavior.

00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:34.634
And now, look,

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:36.769
maybe there's a counterintelligence value

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:39.205
that we see by letting it pass overhead.

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:40.807
Maybe there's there's always more to this

00:05:40.807 --> 00:05:41.908
than, you know, than meets the eye.

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:43.710
And I wouldn't be privy to that now.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.812
So I give the Pentagon some room here.

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:47.947
But those are the big questions

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:49.315
that I think people should ask

00:05:49.315 --> 00:05:50.650
members of Congress should be asking

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:53.319
as they dig into this further.

00:05:53.319 --> 00:05:54.454
What kind of options does

00:05:54.454 --> 00:05:56.189
the US have for responding,

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:57.256
for sending the message

00:05:57.256 --> 00:05:59.726
that you think they should send

00:06:00.827 --> 00:06:02.295
Well, again, first,

00:06:02.295 --> 00:06:02.962
either

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:03.863
capturing the equipment

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:04.497
or shooting it down

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:06.232
would be a strong message.

00:06:06.232 --> 00:06:07.400
There's obviously

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.267
a demarche of the country,

00:06:08.267 --> 00:06:09.502
but we should again

00:06:09.502 --> 00:06:11.404
increase our activities as well.

00:06:11.404 --> 00:06:12.438
You know, recall when Speaker

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:13.906
Pelosi visited

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:16.042
Taiwan last summer, the Chinese ramped up

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:17.610
their crossings

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:19.011
of the Taiwan central line

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:20.947
with both ships and aircraft.

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:22.014
And I never got the sense

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:23.416
that we responded forcefully back.

00:06:23.416 --> 00:06:25.084
You got to match the Chinese

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:25.785
head to head.

00:06:25.785 --> 00:06:27.387
We can't be self deterred

00:06:27.387 --> 00:06:28.988
and we can't let the Chinese Communist

00:06:28.988 --> 00:06:30.723
Party push us around.

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:31.858
They will only respond

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:33.626
to resolve, to commitment.

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:34.894
And we need to show that

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:36.729
when we're facing off against Beijing.

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:37.163
Mark, as

00:06:37.163 --> 00:06:38.364
we were reporting on this yesterday,

00:06:38.364 --> 00:06:39.265
we heard from the Pentagon

00:06:39.265 --> 00:06:39.732
and they say

00:06:39.732 --> 00:06:41.934
this is actually happened before

00:06:42.201 --> 00:06:43.903
during the last administration

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:45.004
when you were defense

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:47.073
secretary, during that time period.

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:48.174
Were you aware of this?

00:06:48.174 --> 00:06:49.342
How was it resolved

00:06:49.342 --> 00:06:50.643
What can you tell us about that?

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:53.846
I read that I was surprised.

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:55.381
I don't ever recall somebody

00:06:55.381 --> 00:06:56.282
coming into my office

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:57.984
or reading anything that

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:58.851
the Chinese had

00:06:58.851 --> 00:07:00.052
a surveillance balloon

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:01.854
above the United States.

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:03.189
And you would obviously know

00:07:03.189 --> 00:07:04.257
that if that had happened

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:06.692
when you were defense secretary.

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:07.894
I would remember that for sure.

00:07:07.894 --> 00:07:09.495
I mean, my focus was on implementing

00:07:09.495 --> 00:07:10.663
the national defense strategy

00:07:10.663 --> 00:07:11.764
to take on the Chinese

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:13.232
as the greatest strategic

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:14.333
threat facing our country.

00:07:14.333 --> 00:07:16.302
So I was keen on everything Chinese.

00:07:16.302 --> 00:07:17.737
We set up a red cell

00:07:17.737 --> 00:07:18.971
within the Pentagon to deal with that.

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:20.173
We reorient

00:07:20.206 --> 00:07:21.974
reoriented the military's doctrine

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:23.443
and how we train and fight

00:07:23.443 --> 00:07:25.144
all those things focused on the Chinese.

00:07:25.144 --> 00:07:27.313
So I would be very curious as to why

00:07:27.313 --> 00:07:28.714
Chinese surveillance balloons

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:30.016
overflying the United States.

00:07:30.016 --> 00:07:31.350
So that would have caught my attention

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:32.084
for sure.

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:33.786
I don't recall it ever happening.

00:07:33.786 --> 00:07:35.188
If you were at the Pentagon

00:07:35.188 --> 00:07:36.322
and this did happen

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:37.323
and the secretary of state

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:39.091
was out to go on a trip to China.

00:07:39.091 --> 00:07:39.926
What would your advice

00:07:39.926 --> 00:07:40.960
to the secretary of state be?

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.295
Would you say, to cancel the trip?

00:07:42.295 --> 00:07:42.795
Would you say

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:43.362
to make sure

00:07:43.362 --> 00:07:45.164
this is the first thing they bring up?

00:07:45.164 --> 00:07:46.165
What would your advice be?

00:07:47.667 --> 00:07:49.202
Well, I suspect Secretary Pompeo

00:07:49.202 --> 00:07:49.936
shared my views

00:07:49.936 --> 00:07:50.303
as well

00:07:50.303 --> 00:07:51.871
with regard to China,

00:07:51.871 --> 00:07:52.972
and I don't know how

00:07:52.972 --> 00:07:53.739
he would have reacted.

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:54.407
I mean,

00:07:54.407 --> 00:07:55.374
sometimes you call off

00:07:55.374 --> 00:07:57.543
trips like this or sometimes you go

00:07:57.543 --> 00:07:59.178
you go prepared to give a very,

00:07:59.178 --> 00:08:00.179
very strong statement

00:08:00.179 --> 00:08:02.215
of of China,

00:08:02.215 --> 00:08:04.016
China violating our sovereignty.

00:08:04.016 --> 00:08:05.084
And so there are different ways

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:05.785
to approach this.

00:08:05.785 --> 00:08:07.053
And it just depends on the broader

00:08:07.053 --> 00:08:08.221
dynamics. And look.

00:08:08.221 --> 00:08:08.754
On the other hand,

00:08:08.754 --> 00:08:10.590
I think the Pentagon made a good move

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.525
with regard to expanding our

00:08:12.525 --> 00:08:13.960
access to Philippine bases.

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:15.027
This was something that

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:15.661
we were working

00:08:15.661 --> 00:08:16.429
on during my tenure

00:08:16.429 --> 00:08:17.430
at the Pentagon, as well as

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.764
how do you expand U.S.

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:20.399
access to bases in the Philippines.

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:21.701
And it's very good

00:08:21.701 --> 00:08:22.335
that we've done that

00:08:22.335 --> 00:08:23.636
because it allows us

00:08:23.636 --> 00:08:24.203
to dress

00:08:24.203 --> 00:08:24.704
to address

00:08:24.704 --> 00:08:25.771
military,

00:08:25.771 --> 00:08:27.173
Chinese military capabilities

00:08:27.173 --> 00:08:28.975
in case war breaks out.

00:08:28.975 --> 00:08:30.877
Do you think in the Indo-Pacific,

00:08:30.877 --> 00:08:32.144
do you think Blinken should cancel

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:32.545
his trip

00:08:34.514 --> 00:08:35.248
That's an option that

00:08:35.248 --> 00:08:36.182
should be considered.

00:08:36.182 --> 00:08:39.051
But I think we need to know more and

00:08:39.051 --> 00:08:40.419
we need to assess what's happening

00:08:40.419 --> 00:08:41.554
in the broader context.

00:08:41.554 --> 00:08:42.455
Curiously,

00:08:42.455 --> 00:08:43.723
the Chinese are not outright

00:08:43.723 --> 00:08:45.224
denying it as they would typically do.

00:08:45.224 --> 00:08:45.858
They're saying, well,

00:08:45.858 --> 00:08:46.659
we would never violate

00:08:46.659 --> 00:08:47.527
someone's sovereignty.

00:08:47.527 --> 00:08:48.895
So the way they're playing

00:08:48.895 --> 00:08:50.763
this is quite curious to me as well.

00:08:50.763 --> 00:08:51.597
What does it say to you

00:08:51.597 --> 00:08:52.965
about the state of U.S.

00:08:52.965 --> 00:08:53.833
China relations

00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:55.368
right now that they would take an act

00:08:55.368 --> 00:08:57.036
that you described as brazen?

00:08:57.036 --> 00:08:58.070
Is this

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:00.139
Well, it's not.

00:09:00.139 --> 00:09:01.941
Well, the relations are not good.

00:09:01.941 --> 00:09:03.175
They have not been good for

00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:03.876
for some time,

00:09:03.876 --> 00:09:05.044
certainly in the months

00:09:05.044 --> 00:09:08.247
leading up to Xi Jinping's

00:09:08.247 --> 00:09:09.849
seizure of its of a third

00:09:09.849 --> 00:09:11.918
term as chairman of the party

00:09:11.918 --> 00:09:12.952
last October.

00:09:12.952 --> 00:09:14.387
But, look, they're not getting better.

00:09:14.387 --> 00:09:16.455
He's he's tried to change his tack

00:09:16.455 --> 00:09:17.223
a little bit,

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:19.825
realizing that Chinese foreign policy

00:09:19.825 --> 00:09:20.927
isn't playing well

00:09:20.927 --> 00:09:22.161
in the international community.

00:09:22.161 --> 00:09:23.596
But I don't think we should be

00:09:25.431 --> 00:09:26.399
I don't think we should be

00:09:26.399 --> 00:09:27.500
fooled by what they're doing.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:28.634
They have an aggressive plan

00:09:28.634 --> 00:09:30.269
to build a modern military

00:09:30.269 --> 00:09:31.137
over the next decade.

00:09:31.137 --> 00:09:31.504
And they

00:09:31.504 --> 00:09:33.673
they stated that their aim by 20, 49

00:09:33.673 --> 00:09:35.141
is to dominate the Indo-Pacific

00:09:35.141 --> 00:09:36.609
if not the global order

00:09:36.609 --> 00:09:38.010
and change the rules and norms.

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.078
And so that is their

00:09:39.078 --> 00:09:40.112
their grand strategy.

00:09:40.112 --> 00:09:41.514
And we need to be cognizant of that

00:09:41.514 --> 00:09:43.249
and do everything we can

00:09:43.249 --> 00:09:44.317
to push back on this,

00:09:44.317 --> 00:09:45.651
to try and change their behavior.

